appears unlikely clark county schools  will return to in-person learning  anytime soon  last night trustees were briefed on the  district's coronavirus response  back in july you'll remember the board  set strict requirements for reopening  schools  those requirements include a five  percent or lower positivity rate  and a downward trend in cases for 14  days  a doctor with the southern nevada health  district said last night clark county  isn't  close to any of those benchmarks however  he says he would  support the board's decision to return  if they have a plan for limiting  capacity  and social distancing board members made  it clear there's no easy answer  would it be more safe for everybody to  keep schools  closed or at least only partially open  um i don't know i just feel really  uncomfortable with this whole thing  and it doesn't seem like there's a lot  of answers and i really don't like the  answer of  just reopen because it's not going to  get better this  year the school board plans to vote on  the future of in-person learning  november 12th
 

